    ],
    "permissions": [
      "patient.merge"
    ],
    "permissions_mode": "all",
    "idempotency_key": false,
    "description": "Workflow §2.4: the temporary trauma record is RETAINED (marked Merged) and all clinical data\ndisplays consolidated under the master. The merged record can no longer be used for new\ntransactions (`PATIENT_MERGED_CANNOT_TRANSACT`). A merge is for good, and a death recorded on the merged profile\nmoves to the master, so:\n\n* a trauma or lab-only profile is merged by the registration desk alone; a **permanent (Regular) profile** (a\n  duplicate) only with a second person who holds `patient.merge.approve` and co-signs at the same terminal\n  (`cosigner_username`, `cosigner_password`): `MERGE_COSIGNER_REQUIRED` without one; `STEP_UP_REQUIRED`,\n  `ACCOUNT_LOCKED` or `DUAL_CONTROL_SAME_PERSON` for a co-signer who cannot co-sign;\n* profiles that name two different people are refused, never overridden: two CNICs, two universal patient medical\n  record numbers (UPMRN), two sexes, two dates of birth, or one seen alive after the other's recorded death: `MERGE_IDENTITY_CONFLICT` (details.conflicts). Correct the\n  wrong profile first.\n\nA CNIC or UPMRN that only the merged profile carried is copied to the master, so the search (which hides merged\nprofiles) still finds the person by it.\n\nAn id in the request body that does not exist: `REFERENCE_NOT_FOUND` (details.field).\n`MERGE_INVALID`: these records cannot be merged.\n\n**Required permission:** `patient.merge`\n\n**Required permission:** `patient.merge`",
    "roles_allowed": [
      "receptionist"
    ],
